       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, 6,400 mg/day is above the labeled maximum, and I'm not able to enter a dose over that limit.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the highest labeled dose, and I can add a note that the specialist recommended escalation.\n- **Suggest other routes.** If standard NSAID dosing hasn't worked, the specialist or pharmacy could consider a different analgesic or an adjunct, such as scheduled acetaminophen up to its own maximum, or a different drug class. Those decisions are yours and theirs to make.\n- **Send the order through pharmacy or the prescriber.** If the above-label dose really is intended, it should go through a pathway with direct prescriber authorization and pharmacist review. That is better than my order entry.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter the 800 mg four times daily order."
      }
